{"Workspace":"/Users/workspace/Workspace/captn","ObservationCache":{"0c39cf79b8e87b16:876268088cc89d6e:053ce7f033d52498:1fb1e4892b9e10e3":{"id":"s1","behavior":"Byte-for-byte identical to s0: the same `parsers` package file defining `ParserNode`, its traversal/accessor methods, `NewParserNode`, the `AttachNode`/`TransformNode` types, `TransformContext` with `Emit`/`WalkChildren`/`WalkChildrenInto`, the default `attach`, and `WalkTransformTree` performing the traced depth-first cursor walk that applies the transform and attaches parents."},"18a6a65d7847294c:0000000000000000:0000000000000000:0000000000000000":{"id":"c0","behavior":"A 'loads' dependency edge: the source-identified entity imports/loads the target entity identified by its hash chain, representing a load/use relationship between the two graph nodes."},"2b1f8ba70960fcb2:f26a61d9717a1672:104876aa1e6bcc60:1fb1e4892b9e10e3":{"id":"s1","behavior":"Identical to s0: the same `cog` package `ObservationGraph` definition with `NewObservationGraph`, `WriteDOT` (deterministic DOT serialization sorted by hash sum, directed/undirected aware), the attribute helpers `observationGraphNodeAttrs`/`observationGraphNodeLabel`/`observationGraphNodeType`/`observationGraphImportType`, the `formatDOTAttrs`/`formatDOTEdgeAttrs` sorted-attribute formatters, `WriteToFile`, and `ExplainWithDepth` which resolves observations into the graph and walks it with `DetailedDFS` to build a per-node/per-edge textual explanation using the `observation-behavior` attributes and node source."},"3409d489d826dfb6:0000000000000000:0000000000000000:0000000000000000":{"id":"c0","behavior":"The main entrypoint depends on (loads) a target component during startup/execution — consistent with main invoking cog.OpenCOG/QuerySnippet to load the COG graph and snippet data before generating an explanation."},"3aec3e37ce45f3bc:389f72be083fd734:c94bfea7452de872:1fb1e4892b9e10e3":{"id":"s1","behavior":"The Go standard library `log` package. Defines the Logger type writing serialized output to an io.Writer (guarded by a mutex), with prefix/flag/isDiscard stored atomically. Provides header-formatting flag constants (Ldate, Ltime, Lmicroseconds, Llongfile, Lshortfile, LUTC, Lmsgprefix, LstdFlags), the New constructor, and a package-level standard logger `std` writing to os.Stderr. Includes the itoa fixed-width decimal helper, formatHeader to compose the prefix/date/time/file:line header, a sync.Pool buffer pool (getBuffer/putBuffer), and the core output method that captures the time, resolves caller file/line via runtime.Caller or a pc, formats, appends a trailing newline if missing, and writes under lock. Exposes Print/Printf/Println, Fatal* (which call os.Exit(1)), and Panic* (which call panic) both as Logger methods and package functions, plus Flags/SetFlags/Prefix/SetPrefix/Output/Writer accessors. init wires internal.DefaultOutput to std.output."},"3ddb7fad020fe2f2:84267d01b4530cbc:9d26959689273038:1fb1e4892b9e10e3":{"id":"s0","behavior":"Go runtime/trace user annotation API (package trace). Defines Task, Region, and the background task plus a context key for carrying tasks. NewTask derives a parent id via fromContext(pctx), allocates a monotonic id with newID() (atomic increment of lastTaskID), emits a UserTaskCreate event, and stores the Task in the returned context. fromContext returns the Task stored under traceContextKey, falling back to bgTask (id 0). Task.End emits UserTaskEnd. Log/Logf emit one-off UserLog events keyed by category (Logf gates on IsEnabled and formats with fmt.Sprintf). WithRegion brackets fn() with userRegion start/end calls; StartRegion returns a noopRegion when tracing is disabled, otherwise emits a start event and returns a Region whose End emits the matching end event. IsEnabled reads tracing.enabled atomically. The userTaskCreate/userTaskEnd/userRegion/userLog functions are declared here but implemented in runtime/trace.go (linkname-style bodies)."},"563f174e12c1f964:d01bdcde40fbba51:521fc4b04c9b3435:c0844a48392406c6":{"id":"s1","behavior":"Body of observationGraphNodeAttrs: copies the input attribute map into a new map sized for 4 extra keys, then defaults 'label' (via observationGraphNodeLabel) only if absent, always sets 'import_type' (via observationGraphImportType using any existing value) and 'file_type' (node.GetLanguage()), and defaults 'node_type' (via observationGraphNodeType) only if absent. Returns the enriched map for DOT node attribute rendering."},"5f61f2e0fdd3b5e2:0000000000000000:0000000000000000:0000000000000000":{"id":"c0","behavior":"Represents a load/dependency relationship where the first symbol loads (opens/reads) the second — consistent with Call invoking cog.OpenCOG to load the COG graph for the working directory before querying and explaining snippets."},"68423a2123f95a68:b50c840326a4aeae:19e990f53abc7596:1fb1e4892b9e10e3":{"id":"s1","behavior":"Identical to s0: the same package mcp `search_and_explain` tool implementation, defining SearchAndExplainInput/Output types, the SearchAndExplainTool with Name/Description/Call, the concurrent grep-search-then-explain pipeline (cog.OpenCOG, grep.Search/SearchSource, dedupeMatches, bounded worker pool of 8, max 32 matches, QuerySnippet + ExplainWithDepth, mutex-collated results, g.Persist), and the dedupeMatches helper plus tool registration."},"6c15bccd614ae849:0000000000000000:0000000000000000:0000000000000000":{"id":"c0","behavior":"A caller in this trace package loads the shared tracing-enabled atomic flag (tracing.enabled.Load()), i.e. the IsEnabled check used to gate tracing work."},"794443e3ce0bb4e0:0000000000000000:0000000000000000:0000000000000000":{"id":"c0","behavior":"Represents the containment/dependency edge in which the enclosing transformer-body block (s1's switch over node.Kind) loads/embeds the referenced AST-construction logic — i.e. the GolangTransformer body is the code that drives emission of the nested AST nodes it constructs."},"861ce7bcdc743d8b:43b1340446644eb7:029e73f819ea924c:5e8e62e02d84bcf7":{"id":"s0","behavior":"Defines the `parsers` package's tree-sitter abstraction layer. `ParserNode` wraps a `*tree_sitter.Node` plus its `common.Source`, `Kind`, and `Range`, decoupling callers from tree-sitter directly. Accessor/traversal methods: `GetSource`, `Debug` (S-expression dump), `GetPosition` (builds a `common.FileRange` from the node's start/end row/column/byte), `IterateChildren` (iterates named children, stopping on error or when the iterator returns false), `GetNthChildByKind` (returns the n-th named child matching a kind), `IterateChildrenByFieldName` (iterates named children matching a field name), `ChildByFieldName` (single named child by field name), and `GetTextContent` (UTF-8 text from the source buffer). A compile-time assertion confirms `*ParserNode` satisfies `ast.ASTParserNode`. `NewParserNode` constructs a ParserNode from a source and raw node. Declares function types `AttachNode` and `TransformNode`, and a `TransformContext` holding the cursor, root `ASTModule`, current `Parent`, attach func, and walk func, with `Emit`/`WalkChildren`/`WalkChildrenInto` helpers. The default `attach` appends a child to its parent. `WalkTransformTree` drives a depth-first tree-sitter cursor walk: for each node it invokes the `transform` callback inside a `runtime/trace` region/task, manages `trx.Parent` save/restore as it recurses, and finally calls `ast.AttachParents(root)` to wire up parent pointers."},"92c375d99efb8f05:0000000000000000:0000000000000000:0000000000000000":{"id":"c1","behavior":"A second 'loads' dependency edge from the same source entity to a different target entity, indicating it also loads/imports that node in the observation graph."},"958fc5d384b07e59:f93530ecb8bd0b39:88243b550f35e630:5e8e62e02d84bcf7":{"id":"s0","behavior":"Defines the `cog` package's `ObservationGraph`, a wrapper around `cgraph.Graph[common.HashType, COGNode]`. `NewObservationGraph` constructs it. `WriteDOT` serializes the graph to Graphviz DOT: it picks `strict graph`/`--` or `strict digraph`/`-\u003e` based on `Graph.Traits().IsDirected`, fetches the adjacency map, sorts vertices and per-vertex targets by `HashType.Sum()` for deterministic output, and emits each vertex (with computed attributes and `weight=0`) followed by its edges (with edge weight and attributes). `observationGraphNodeAttrs` copies existing attrs and fills in `label`, `import_type`, `file_type` (from node language), and `node_type`. `observationGraphNodeLabel` uses a `fmt.Stringer` if implemented, else the file base name, else the Go type. `observationGraphNodeType` returns an `ast.ASTNode.Kind()` when applicable, else the type. `observationGraphImportType` classifies the dependency: honors an existing `common.DependencyType` value (local/stdlib/package→\"dependency\"), otherwise inspects the cleaned slash path for Go toolchain stdlib, `/pkg/mod/` or `/vendor/` (\"dependency\"), defaulting to local. `formatDOTAttrs`/`formatDOTEdgeAttrs` render sorted key/quoted-value attribute strings (node attrs trailing-comma style, edge attrs leading-comma style). `WriteToFile` creates a file and writes DOT to it. `ExplainWithDepth` validates non-nil `cog` and root node, calls `prov.ResolveObservationsToGraph` to populate the graph, dumps the graph to `./graph.gv`, then runs `Graph.DetailedDFS` from the root hash building a textual explanation: per node it appends the file path, the `observation-behavior` attribute, language, and source code; for nodes with a parent it appends the edge's `observation-behavior` and a sentence relating parent and child file paths. Returns the accumulated explanation string."},"a92a2a5cded124b0:30ce1a33dc57a417:4503e35550a20c69:c0844a48392406c6":{"id":"s1","behavior":"Body of GolangTransformer: a switch on node.Kind mapping tree-sitter Go grammar nodes to emitted AST entities. `package_clause` sets the module root Name from the package_identifier. `import_spec` builds an ASTImportStatement, setting optional Namespace from the `name` field and Reference from the interpreted_string_literal_content of the `path`; only emits when a Reference exists. `function_declaration`/`method_declaration` create an ASTFuncExpression with Name and (non-parameter_list) ReturnType, attach the inner `block` as its Block, emit it, then WalkChildrenInto so params/body land under it. `func_literal` does the same minus the Name. `parameter_list` (only when the transform Parent is an ASTFuncExpression) iterates parameter_declaration children, extracting name/type symbols into ASTFuncArgument entries appended to fn.Arguments. `short_var_decl` builds an ASTDeclaration collecting all `left`-field identifiers as Names and walks into it so RHS calls are captured. `var_spec` similarly collects the single `name`. `call_expression` builds an ASTCallExpression: for selector_expression function it sets Namespace from an identifier operand and Symbol from the field, for plain identifier it sets Symbol; it flattens argument_list identifiers via collectIdentifiers into ASTFuncArgument entries (empty arg when none), emits, then walks children to handle chained calls. `return_statement` captures plain identifier return values as child symbols. `comment` is intentionally skipped. Default just WalkChildren."},"af6c4e57190e79fd:7ae82f502f0c9005:7d155054ad97484e:5e8e62e02d84bcf7":{"id":"s0","behavior":"Defines the CLI entrypoint (package main) using kong to parse a CLI struct with two commands: `run \u003cpath\u003e \u003csnippet\u003e` and `claude`. For `claude`: starts an MCP server on localhost:10580 via mcp.StartServer, marshals a Claude MCP config (mcp.NewClaudeMCPConfig/NewClaudeMCPServer) pointing the 'captn' server at http://localhost:10580, then execs the external `claude` binary with an appended system prompt instructing it to use the MCP explain tool instead of the Read tool, wiring stdio through. For `run`: enables runtime/trace into trace.out, opens a COG graph from the CWD via cog.OpenCOG, creates a ClaudeCodeProvider, queries a snippet with g.QuerySnippet, calls og.ExplainWithDepth(depth 1) to generate an explanation, prints it, and persists the graph with g.Persist. Default case panics with the command name. Fatal errors are logged via log.Fatalf or panics."},"b3223350090b8fe0:0000000000000000:0000000000000000:0000000000000000":{"id":"c1","behavior":"The main entrypoint also loads a second target component — consistent with main pulling in another dependency (e.g. the MCP server setup or the Claude provider/explanation pipeline) used to fulfill the requested command."},"b4211d1091fcad34:5a86420193525757:8cf4c87a9d5e3acb:5e8e62e02d84bcf7":{"id":"s0","behavior":"Defines the MCP `search_and_explain` tool in package mcp. SearchAndExplainTool.Call gets the CWD, opens a COG graph via cog.OpenCOG, and creates a Claude Code provider. It searches source with grep.Search (when Include is empty) or grep.SearchSource (with the include pattern) for the given Snippet. Matches are deduplicated by path+text via dedupeMatches and capped at maxSearchMatches (32). Each surviving match is processed concurrently through a bounded worker pool (sem of size searchExplainWorker=8): it converts the path to a CWD-relative path, calls g.QuerySnippet to resolve the snippet, then og.ExplainWithDepth(depth 1) to generate an explanation; failures skip that match silently. Successful results are appended under a mutex into SearchAndExplainOutputItem entries. After wg.Wait it persists the COG (g.Persist) and returns SearchAndExplainOutput. Includes input/output structs with jsonschema tags, constructor helpers, and registers searchAndExplainTool as a Tool[SearchAndExplainInput, SearchAndExplainOutput]."},"bdb1395c6439e7f4:f313fde91751ec78:3d2816b28c3b797d:c0844a48392406c6":{"id":"s2","behavior":"The body of main from s0: parses the kong CLI and switches on the command. The `claude` branch starts the MCP server, builds and marshals the Claude MCP config, and execs the external claude binary with stdio attached. The `run \u003cpath\u003e \u003csnippet\u003e` branch sets up runtime tracing, opens the COG graph from the CWD, builds a ClaudeCodeProvider, queries the snippet, produces a depth-1 explanation, prints it, and persists the graph; the default branch panics with the command string."},"c35e52c431375e51:0000000000000000:0000000000000000:0000000000000000":{"id":"c0","behavior":"The first symbol reads/loads the value or resource defined by the second symbol, establishing a load (read) dependency from the former on the latter."},"d97998c1ceb7b521:0000000000000000:0000000000000000:0000000000000000":{"id":"c0","behavior":"A `loads` dependency: the first symbol references/uses the second. Given the shared package, this reflects one of the file's functions (e.g. `WalkTransformTree` or a `ParserNode` method) invoking another (e.g. `NewParserNode`, `attach`, or `ast.AttachParents`), wiring the cursor-walk transform pipeline together."},"e90390d3144aec75:0000000000000000:0000000000000000:0000000000000000":{"id":"c1","behavior":"A second caller loads the same shared tracing-enabled atomic flag, reusing the IsEnabled/enabled.Load gate before doing trace work."},"ea4a8a9737b4492c:55876bc26fe74888:06be04ed3fa8c3ef:5e8e62e02d84bcf7":{"id":"s0","behavior":"Defines the Go language support for the captn parser in package languages_golang. Exposes GolangLanguageSupportDefinition implementing a language-support interface: GetLanguageID returns \"go\"; GetTreeSitterLanguage returns the tree-sitter-go grammar; Parse builds an ASTModule root and runs parsers.WalkTransformTree with GolangTransformer; NewLSPServer resolves GOPATH via `go env GOPATH`, launches the gopls binary from $GOPATH/bin/gopls wired to stdin/stdout pipes and wraps it in lsp.NewServerProcess; ClassifyImportType cleans the source path and uses regexes to label it StandardLibraryDependency (toolchain stdlib under pkg/mod/golang.org/toolchain@.../src/), PackageDependency (vendor/ or pkg/mod cache), otherwise LocalDependency. Helper collectIdentifiers recursively gathers all `identifier` nodes into ASTSymbols. GolangTransformer is a per-node visitor that converts tree-sitter Go nodes into AST constructs (package name, imports, functions/methods, func literals, parameters, declarations, call expressions, returns). Two TODOs note go embeds and comments are unsupported."}}}